Third-party components
----------------------

This release bundles no third-party source and links no third-party library.

The core libraries under libs/ depend on the C++17 standard library and on
platform system calls only.

The HTTP client dependency that libs/usd-asset-http will own has been chosen:
libcurl (https://curl.se), under the curl license, an MIT/X11 derivative that
places no constraint on redistribution of a plugin binary. The decision and its
grounds are docs/adr/0003-http-client-dependency.md; the criteria it was made
against are docs/design/DESIGN_POLICY.md §13. No libcurl code is bundled here
and none is linked yet — it is acquired through find_package, and it arrives
with the first libs/usd-asset-http commit in v0.2.0. Its copyright notice and
license text are recorded in this file at that point.

OpenUSD (https://openusd.org), which the plugin bundle under plugins/ links
against from v0.2.0, is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 with the
modifications noted in its own NOTICE file. It is a runtime dependency of the
bundle only; nothing under libs/ links it.
